Your task: elaborate an HLR into one or more Low-Level Requirements (LLRs) scoped to a specific MODULE.
{% include "shared/tool_reminder.j2" %} {% include "shared/node_id_format.j2" %}
{% include "shared/multi_write_tip.j2" %}

Steps:
1. graph_read — find HLR nodes that have no LLR children.
2. graph_read — find the MODULE(s) that trace to this HLR for context.
3. derive_requirement(parent_content=<HLR text>, level='llr') — can help refine the HLR text into an LLR. Returns {req_text, verification_method}.
4. graph_add_node — create LLR node(s):
   - node_type = LLR
   - parent_id = the HLR node ID
   - content = refined requirement sentence
   - title = 3–5 words
   - No trace_to on LLR nodes.

One LLR per atomic behaviour is preferred. Do not create duplicate LLRs for the same behaviour.
